			<div class="content" id="post-content-2347802">
									

<p>I have no issue with the writing itself, and I like the core idea of an entity that hunts, consumes, and replaces negative dream imagery. That could go in some pretty wild places.</p>
<p>Dream-based articles are difficult to write in my experience, especially in a manner that's intended to be an informative document for an organization's records. Dream imagery is amorphous and impenetrable. This makes it ideal for experimental prose and surrealistic exercises, but it also means that it's very difficult to write something relating the experiences of another person, much less a common experience between multiple people.</p>
<p>I won't say that something like this can't work in the SCP format, but I do think the documentation needs to delve a little more deeply (I would prefer much deeper, personally) into what this thing is and what it does to people for it to really take advantage of the starting concept. There's the beginnings of something really good here, but I don't think it's there yet.</p>

							</div>

								
					
