<p>There are several problems with the writing. It's awkward as a general rule, but a few things stick out.</p>
<p>First of all, &quot;nonviolent D-class&quot; sent out a red flag. D-Class are, at least allegedly, criminals on death row. &quot;Are permitted entertainment material as requested&quot; is vague, and sounds as though they can have anything they want without limitation. &quot;While still asleep, hosts realize and understand that they are dreaming, but also an understanding that they are entirely safe,&quot; is grammatically incorrect.</p>
<p>But also the Special Containment Procedures don't make sense. It's a thing that cures night terrors and wants to protect people from nightmares (sort of like Snoozee if he actually did his damn job). But why do we need three people to contain this? It can't leave if no one's sleeping within 100 meters of it, it's dormant when the person isn't asleep, and seems to be largely benevolent. There's no reason to use more than one person to contain it.</p>
<p>Downvoted.</p>

