					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dexanote" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(481882); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=481882&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607849602" alt="Dexanote" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=481882)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/dexanote" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(481882); return false;" >Dexanote</a></span> <span class="odate time_1438492754 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Aug 2015 05:19</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2350296">
									

<p>While its a headcanon-to-headcanon thing, I don't think all D-Class are violent criminals. Hell, in some SCPs you can't have violent criminals dealing with the object.</p>
<p>Non-violent D-Class are just people the Foundation has acquired or demoted to the role, whether criminial or not. I can't really tell you to cancel downvote for that (as you have more reasons than just that to downvote) but frankly its not unheard of and opens up the opportunity for some D-Class to be random people abducted by the Men In Black and experimented with. Which is a twist on the classic MIB urban legend, which fits with the basic idea of the Foundation (and is exactly what I use as a feature in my articles).</p>
<p>Using three people allows it to cycle between the three in a predictable pattern, allowing for regular tests as it moves from an 'empty' host to a &quot;full&quot; one.</p>
<p>Say Host A has held the SCP for a few days, and is having clean, restful dreams each night because of it. Meanwhile, Host B hasn't held 2840 for two weeks now, and is beginning to have her regular terrors again. So they can then guess when 2840 will jump to Host B, measuring the intensity of the dreams that it seems to be attracted to. Host C has begun to have unpleasant dreams as well, but won't be quite 'tasty' enough to attract 2840 for a while, allowing them to study Host B while Host C's condition continues returning to its baseline, and Host A is allowed a brief reprieve from his nightmares after 2840 'cleansed' him.</p>
<p>Otherwise, yes, it is rather awkward in parts, thats a weakness of my own. I'm going to update it soon. EVERYONE has told me its missing something, I need to find what.</p>

							</div>

								
					
