				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/highroller" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2220195); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2220195&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607849602" alt="Highroller" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2220195)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/highroller" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2220195); return false;" >Highroller</a></span> <span class="odate time_1438494359 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">02 Aug 2015 05:45</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2350302">
									

<p>But that's just it: it cannot jump from its host to anyone else unless you specifically put another person there and have them sleep within 100 meters of each other. It doesn't matter where it gravitates to, it's specifically got a 100 meter jumping ability. Based on the rules you've set up regarding this SCP, the containment procedures don't make sense. Now, maybe, since this thing &quot;eats&quot; nightmares, it needs to feed or it will starve to death? But that needs to be included.</p>
<p>Now, the concept of a beneficial creature who wants to protect people from nightmares, or just happens to have bad dreams as its natural food source, has potential as an idea. The thing I think is missing, and what will probably help once you get that down, is a sense of tone. This creature is inherently the opposite of scary - it's a thing that helps make scary things go away - so what do you want the audience to feel if not fear?</p>
<p>I think once you get that down, the rest will flow from there.</p>

							</div>

								
